# Line endings are normalised to LF in the repository, whatever the contributor's
# platform does in their working copy.
#
# This is not cosmetic. Everything that runs in CI runs on Linux: the `run:` blocks in
# .github/workflows are executed by bash, and a stray CR at the end of a line there is a
# syntax error rather than whitespace. Today the tree is LF because the people who wrote
# it happened to have core.autocrlf=true; without a rule in the repository, one
# contributor with a different setting can commit CRLF into a workflow or a script and
# break the build for everyone, with a diff that looks empty.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicit for the files where a CR is fatal rather than untidy.
*.sh      text eol=lf
*.py      text eol=lf
*.yml     text eol=lf
*.yaml    text eol=lf
*.toml    text eol=lf
*.rs      text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf

# Binary: never translated, never diffed as text.
*.png     binary
*.jpg     binary
*.jpeg    binary
*.gif     binary
*.ico     binary
*.mp4     binary
*.tar.gz  binary
*.zip     binary
